  "title": "Convert blocked to unclear only on positive evidence that this invocation's browser worked",
  "detail": "The rest matches #860: markers, prompt, conversion order, feedback, resume and legacy loading all check out, and source is 109 lines against 180. One gap is against spec requirement 3, which requires the engine's same-attempt records to show successful browser setup.\n\n`engine.ts:2378` treats the absence of a `browser_unavailable` warning as success. But `browserMcp` (`src/harness/browser-mcp.ts:252`) only builds the launch configuration, and a later MCP startup or handshake failure reaches the run as ordinary stderr (`src/harness/codex.ts:984`). In that case the verifier returns `blocked`, the engine records `available`, converts the row to `unclear`, and sends implementation feedback for an infrastructure failure.\n\nFix: treat browser setup as successful for an invocation only when that invocation's own recorded events include a successful browser tool result. That means a call to one of the granted Playwright MCP tools that returned without an error. Derive it from the events the harness already records for that invocation id, never from the verifier's output text. With no such event, a blocked browser check keeps today's infrastructure handling, including the existing single alternate-model environment retry. Don't add MCP handshake parsing to the harnesses in this slice.\n\nTests, all fakes:\n1. Preview ready and configuration valid, but no browser tool result in the invocation (the handshake failed): `blocked` stays `blocked`, with environment handling and no implementation feedback.\n2. A successful browser tool result in the same invocation: `blocked` becomes `unclear`, as today.\n3. Invocation transition: invocation 0 has no browser evidence, and invocation 1 has a successful browser tool result. Only invocation 1's row converts. Removing the invocation-id filter at `engine.ts:2381` must fail this test; today all 105 tests pass without it.\nEach test fails with its guard removed."
 }
